    <string name="calib_title">Double-sided calibration</string>
    <string name="calib_intro">Once per tray we find out how the sheet goes back in so the second side lands on the back, the right way up. Usually one sheet is enough — if a number lands on the same side, its blank back is used next.</string>
    <string name="calib_saved">Saved: %1$s</string>
    <string name="calib_step1">Step 1 · number one</string>
    <string name="calib_step1_body">Put blank paper into %1$s and tap Print one. A sheet with a big 1 and an arrow at the top edge comes out.</string>
    <string name="calib_print1">Print number one</string>
    <string name="calib_printing">Printing side %1$d…</string>
    <string name="calib_step2">Step 2 · put the sheet back</string>
    <string name="calib_step2_body">Take the sheet from the output and put it into %1$s %2$s, arrow (top edge) first into the printer. In the cassette lay it on top of the other paper.</string>
    <string name="calib_print2">Print number two</string>
    <string name="calib_print_n">Print %1$d</string>
    <string name="calib_step2_n">Put the sheet back · then %1$d prints</string>
    <string name="calib_do_first">1. Take the sheet with %1$s from the printer output.\n2. Turn it %2$s.\n3. The arrow must point into the printer — away from you, as in the picture.\n4. Put it into %3$s (on top of the paper in a cassette) and tap Print %4$d.</string>
    <string name="calib_do_reuse">1. Take the sheet (numbers %1$s) from the printer output.\n2. Turn it %2$s — the other way than last time.\n3. The arrow must point into the printer — away from you, as in the picture.\n4. Put it into %3$s (on top of the paper in a cassette) and tap Print %4$d.</string>
    <string name="calib_face_up_do">numbers UP (you see them)</string>
    <string name="calib_face_down_do">numbers DOWN (you see the blank back)</string>
